Introduced the `clarity-kernel` crate, the first step of extracting the consensus-shared Clarity runtime out of the `clarity` VM crate. Moved so far, with all previous `clarity::vm::...` paths preserved via re-exports: the event types (`vm::events`); the pure execution-cost layer (`ExecutionCost`, `CostErrors`, `CostTracker`, `ClarityCostFunction`/`CostValues`, and the `costs_1`–`costs_5` cost-function implementations); the shared error vocabulary (`vm::errors` minus `ClarityEvalError`, `vm::analysis::errors`, `vm::diagnostic`); and the database layer (`ClarityDatabase`, `ClarityBackingStore`, rollback machinery, `HeadersDB`/`BurnStateDB`). Engine-side pieces stay in `clarity`: contract storage now goes through the `ClarityDatabaseExt` extension trait (external callers of `get_contract`/`insert_contract`/`load_contract_analysis`/`get_contract_size` need to import it), `as_analysis_db` moved to the `AsAnalysisDb` extension trait, the special-case handler is carried by the kernel as an opaque token with the concrete `SpecialCaseHandlerFn` type defined in `clarity` (hosts wrap their handler in a `static`), and the execution cache is attached as an opaque engine-owned slot. Behavior is unchanged. `AssetMap` also moved to `clarity_kernel::assets` (re-exported from its old paths). The kernel now additionally defines the v0 engine ABI (`clarity_kernel::engine`): the `Engine` trait, `TransactionContext`, execution outcomes, `EngineError`, and the (not yet wired) `ContractDispatcher`; the interpreter is available behind it as `clarity::vm::engine::LegacyEngine`, demonstrated by a standalone embedder example (`cargo run -p clarity --example embedder`). The ABI meters execution costs (`CostBudget::Limited` enforced cumulatively per transaction context, consumed cost reported in outcomes) and `LegacyEngine::deploy_contract` runs the full parse → persisted static analysis → evaluation pipeline. The stored contract-interface format is now kernel-owned: `FunctionType`/`FunctionSignature` and the `ContractInterface` (JSON ABI) types moved to `clarity-kernel` (the type checkers' `impl FunctionType` blocks became the `FunctionTypeExt`/`FunctionTypeExtV21`/`FunctionTypeExtV205` extension traits), and contract analyses are persisted via `clarity_kernel::analysis::StoredContractAnalysis`, a serde-exact mirror of the previous format (byte-identity enforced by test). `StoredContractAnalysis::load` provides engine-agnostic access to deployed contract interfaces. The engine ABI expresses the production transaction flow: phased deploys (`analyze_contract` → `initialize_contract` → `save_analysis`, matching the node's smart-contract processing order), post-condition-style abort callbacks (`EngineError::AbortedByCallback` with receipt data), and resource budgets (`ResourceBudget` moved to `clarity-kernel` and threaded through the ABI).
